  'openapi: "3.1.0"\ninfo:\n  title: Mzizi API\n  version: "1.0.0"\n  description: |\n    The Mzizi API — components, brand, architecture, Ubuntu doctrine, the open DNA-helix frontend\n    model, and design system. Mzizi owns and operates the registry and this API. It is an\n    open-architecture project of the Bundu Foundation.\n\n    The Mzizi API follows resource-oriented design principles. All resources\n    are served as JSON with schema.org JSON-LD metadata, CORS headers, and CDN-friendly caching.\n\n    **Files are the data layer.** Every route answers from the files in\n    [mzizi-dev/mzizi-registry](https://github.com/mzizi-dev/mzizi-registry): `registry.json`,\n    the component sources on disk, `content/doctrine/**` and the generated `lib/*` modules. There\n    is no database behind this API. Data that is not in those files, such as component version\n    history, is not served here.\n\n    **Base URL:** `https://api.mzizi.dev/v1`\n\n    **Registry:** every item across the nodes and rungs of the Mzizi DNA double helix, read from\n    `registry.json` and the files on disk. The live count is `meta.registryTotal` on `GET /v1/ui`;\n    counts are never hardcoded in this spec, so it cannot drift from the registry.\n\n    **MCP Server:** `https://mcp.mzizi.dev/mcp` (Streamable HTTP transport; `mzizi.dev/mcp` 308-redirects here)\n  contact:\n    name: Mzizi\n  license:\n    name: MIT\n    identifier: MIT\n\nservers:\n  - url: https://api.mzizi.dev/v1\n    description: Production\n  - url: http://localhost:3000/api/v1\n    description: Development\n\ntags:\n  - name: Discovery\n    description: API metadata, health, search, stats\n  - name: Brand\n    description: |\n      The Mzizi brand system: 21 colour families (7 minerals, 7 heritage tones, 7 experimental\n      tones), each with its `-text` values, plus typography, spacing and the ecosystem brands\n  - name: Registry\n    description: Component registry (shadcn-compatible)\n  - name: Architecture\n    description: Ecosystem architecture, data layer, pipeline, sovereignty, the DNA-helix frontend model\n  - name: Ubuntu\n    description: Ubuntu doctrine — Five Pillars and Five Principles\n  - name: Content\n    description: Documentation pages, changelog, AI instructions\n  - name: MCP\n    description: Model Context Protocol server for AI assistants\n\npaths:\n  /:\n    get:\n      summary: API Discovery\n      description: Returns a discovery document listing all available resources.\n      operationId: getApiDiscovery\n      tags: [Discovery]\n      responses:\n        "200":\n          description: Discovery document with schema.org WebAPI metadata\n          headers:\n            Cache-Control:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CachePublic"\n            Access-Control-Allow-Origin:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CorsWildcard"\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: "#/components/schemas/ApiDiscovery"\n        "500":\n          $ref: "#/components/responses/InternalError"\n\n  /brand:\n    get:\n      summary: Brand System\n      description: |\n        Returns the complete Mzizi brand system: the 21 colour families (7 minerals, 7 heritage\n        tones, 7 experimental tones), typography, spacing, ecosystem brands, accessibility\n        standards, and voice & tone.\n\n        Every colour family carries its `-text` values, `textLight` and `textDark`: the colour\n        to use for text in that family on the page (`--color-<name>-text`). `lightHex` and\n        `darkHex` are the canonical accents, not text values. Minerals and experimental tones\n        also carry `onContainerLight` / `onContainerDark`, the text colour on their container.\n\n        Includes schema.org JSON-LD metadata (`@context`, `@type: Brand`).\n      operationId: getBrandSystem\n      tags: [Brand]\n      responses:\n        "200":\n          description: Complete brand system\n          headers:\n            Cache-Control:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CachePublic"\n            Access-Control-Allow-Origin:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CorsWildcard"\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: "#/components/schemas/BrandSystem"\n        "500":\n          $ref: "#/components/responses/InternalError"\n\n  /ui:\n    get:\n      summary: Component Registry Index\n      description: |\n        Returns metadata for every registry item across the Mzizi DNA double helix, from\n        `registry.json` and the files on disk. `meta.registryTotal` is the live count.\n      operationId: getRegistryIndex\n      tags: [Registry]\n      responses:\n        "200":\n          description: Registry index\n          headers:\n            Cache-Control:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CachePublic"\n            Access-Control-Allow-Origin:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CorsWildcard"\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: "#/components/schemas/RegistryIndex"\n        "500":\n          $ref: "#/components/responses/InternalError"\n\n  /ui/{name}:\n    get:\n      summary: Individual Component\n      description: |\n        Returns a single component with inline source code, read from `registry.json` and the\n        component\'s file on disk.\n      operationId: getComponent\n      tags: [Registry]\n      parameters:\n        - name: name\n          in: path\n          required: true\n          description: Component name in kebab-case (e.g., "button", "use-toast")\n          schema:\n            type: string\n            pattern: "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$"\n          examples:\n            ui:\n              value: button\n              summary: A UI component\n            hook:\n              value: use-toast\n              summary: A hook\n            lib:\n              value: utils\n              summary: A library utility\n      responses:\n        "200":\n          description: Component with source code\n          headers:\n            Cache-Control:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CachePublic"\n            Access-Control-Allow-Origin:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CorsWildcard"\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: "#/components/schemas/RegistryItem"\n        "400":\n          description: Invalid component name\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: "#/components/schemas/Error"\n        "404":\n          description: Component not found\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: "#/components/schemas/Error"\n        "500":\n          $ref: "#/components/responses/InternalError"\n\n  /astro:\n    get:\n      summary: Astro Implementations\n      description: |\n        Every name with an Astro implementation (mzizi-registry#397): a pure `.astro` file beside\n        the component\'s `.tsx` (and `.rs`), or a framework-free `.ts` module the `.astro` files\n        import. Install one with `npx @nyuchi/mzizi-cli add <name> --target astro`.\n      operationId: listAstro\n      tags: [Registry]\n      responses:\n        "200":\n          description: The Astro names, each with its document URL\n          headers:\n            Cache-Control:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CachePublic"\n            Access-Control-Allow-Origin:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CorsWildcard"\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                properties:\n                  target:\n                    type: string\n                    enum: [astro]\n                  install:\n                    type: string\n                  count:\n                    type: integer\n                  components:\n                    type: array\n                    items:\n                      type: object\n                      properties:\n                        name:\n                          type: string\n                        url:\n                          type: string\n                          format: uri\n\n  /astro/{name}:\n    get:\n      summary: Astro Implementation\n      description: |\n        The Astro implementation of a component, as a registry document an installer writes into\n        `src/components/mzizi/`. Pure Astro: no React or other framework under it, and no client\n        JavaScript unless the component\'s contract allows one enhancement script. Its\n        `registryDependencies` are absolute `/v1/astro/` URLs derived from the source\'s flat imports\n        (`./button.astro`, `./ui-utils`); its bare imports are its npm `dependencies`; a brand asset\n        it imports ships beside it as a `registry:asset` file with `encoding: base64`.\n      operationId: getAstroComponent\n      tags: [Registry]\n      parameters:\n        - name: name\n          in: path\n          required: true\n          description: Component name in kebab-case (e.g., "app-data-table", "button", "ui-utils")\n          schema:\n            type: string\n            pattern: "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$"\n      responses:\n        "200":\n          description: The Astro document\n          headers:\n            Cache-Control:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CachePublic"\n            Access-Control-Allow-Origin:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CorsWildcard"\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [name, type, target, dependencies, registryDependencies, files]\n                properties:\n                  name:\n                    type: string\n                  type:\n                    type: string\n                    enum: [registry:astro, registry:lib]\n                  target:\n                    type: string\n                    enum: [astro]\n                  title:\n                    type: string\n                  description:\n                    type: string\n                  dependencies:\n                    type: array\n                    items:\n                      type: string\n                  registryDependencies:\n                    type: array\n                    items:\n                      type: string\n                      format: uri\n                  files:\n                    type: array\n                    items:\n                      type: object\n                      required: [path, type, target, content]\n                      properties:\n                        path:\n                          type: string\n                        type:\n                          type: string\n                          enum: [registry:astro, registry:lib, registry:asset]\n                        target:\n                          type: string\n                        content:\n                          type: string\n                        encoding:\n                          type: string\n                          enum: [base64]\n        "404":\n          description: Unknown component, or a component with no Astro implementation\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: "#/components/schemas/Error"\n\n  /ecosystem:\n    get:\n      summary: Ecosystem Architecture\n      description: |\n        Returns architecture principles (Ubuntu, local-first, mobile-first,\n        open-source/sovereign, open-data) and the framework decision (Next.js + Capacitor).\n\n        Includes schema.org JSON-LD metadata (`@context`, `@type: TechArticle`).\n      operationId: getEcosystem\n      tags: [Architecture]\n      responses:\n        "200":\n          description: Ecosystem architecture\n          headers:\n            Cache-Control:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CachePublic"\n            Access-Control-Allow-Origin:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CorsWildcard"\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: "#/components/schemas/EcosystemArchitecture"\n        "500":\n          $ref: "#/components/responses/InternalError"\n\n  /data-layer:\n    get:\n      summary: Data Layer Architecture\n      description: |\n        Returns the local-first data layer (RxDB, SQLite, IndexedDB),\n        cloud services (Supabase, CouchDB), and data ownership rules.\n\n        Includes schema.org JSON-LD metadata (`@context`, `@type: TechArticle`).\n      operationId: getDataLayer\n      tags: [Architecture]\n      responses:\n        "200":\n          description: Data layer specification\n          headers:\n            Cache-Control:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CachePublic"\n            Access-Control-Allow-Origin:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CorsWildcard"\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: "#/components/schemas/DataLayerArchitecture"\n        "500":\n          $ref: "#/components/responses/InternalError"\n\n  /pipeline:\n    get:\n      summary: Open Data Pipeline\n      description: |\n        Returns the open data pipeline stages — Redpanda event streaming,\n        Apache Flink PII stripping, and Apache Doris analytics.\n\n        Includes schema.org JSON-LD metadata (`@context`, `@type: TechArticle`).\n      operationId: getPipeline\n      tags: [Architecture]\n      responses:\n        "200":\n          description: Pipeline stages\n          headers:\n            Cache-Control:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CachePublic"\n            Access-Control-Allow-Origin:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CorsWildcard"\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: "#/components/schemas/PipelineArchitecture"\n        "500":\n          $ref: "#/components/responses/InternalError"\n\n  /sovereignty:\n    get:\n      summary: Technology Sovereignty\n      description: |\n        Returns sovereignty assessments for every technology in the stack,\n        including removed technologies and migration notes.\n\n        Includes schema.org JSON-LD metadata (`@context`, `@type: TechArticle`).\n      operationId: getSovereignty\n      tags: [Architecture]\n      responses:\n        "200":\n          description: Sovereignty assessments\n          headers:\n            Cache-Control:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CachePublic"\n            Access-Control-Allow-Origin:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CorsWildcard"\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: "#/components/schemas/SovereigntyReport"\n        "500":\n          $ref: "#/components/responses/InternalError"\n\n  /health:\n    get:\n      summary: Health Check\n      description: |\n        Returns structured health status for monitoring.\n        Compatible with Vercel, Datadog, and standard health check protocols.\n        No caching — always returns live status.\n      operationId: getHealth\n      tags: [Discovery]\n      responses:\n        "200":\n          description: All checks passing\n          headers:\n            Cache-Control:\n              schema:\n                type: string\n                example: "no-cache, no-store"\n            Access-Control-Allow-Origin:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CorsWildcard"\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: "#/components/schemas/HealthStatus"\n        "503":\n          description: One or more checks failing\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: "#/components/schemas/HealthStatus"\n\n  /architecture:\n    get:\n      summary: Architecture snapshot (DNA double helix)\n      description: |\n        Full snapshot of the Mzizi DNA double helix — every node and rung with its\n        covenant, stakeholder, implementation rules and live component count, plus the\n        strands that group them by backbone. There are no axes and no outliers.\n\n        Reads the helix doctrine under `content/doctrine/` in the registry, with each node\'s\n        component count derived from where the component files live on disk.\n\n        `data` is an object with `nodes`, `rungs`, and `strands` arrays. An empty model\n        returns 200 with empty arrays and `meta.empty: true`, so a consumer can\n        distinguish "the collection is empty" from "the request failed"; nothing is\n        substituted from a fallback. ISR cache: 1 hour.\n      operationId: getArchitectureSnapshot\n      tags: [Architecture]\n      responses:\n        "200":\n          description: "Snapshot of the helix — strands with their nodes, plus the rungs."\n          headers:\n            Cache-Control:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CachePublic"\n            Access-Control-Allow-Origin:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CorsWildcard"\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                properties:\n                  data:\n                    type: object\n                    properties:\n                      nodes:\n                        type: array\n                        items: {type: object}\n                      rungs:\n                        type: array\n                        items: {type: object}\n                      strands:\n                        type: array\n                        items: {type: object}\n                  meta:\n                    type: object\n                    properties:\n                      model: {type: string, example: mzizi-dna-helix}\n                      node_count: {type: integer}\n                      rung_count: {type: integer}\n                      strand_count: {type: integer}\n                      empty:\n                        type: boolean\n                        description: >-\n                          True when the collection returned nothing. The\n                          response is still 200 with empty arrays — an empty\n                          model is reported honestly rather than filled with a\n                          fallback.\n                      source: {type: string}\n                      version: {type: string}\n\n  /architecture/axes:\n    get:\n      summary: Per-axis summary (retired)\n      description: |\n        **HTTP 410 Gone — retired.** The axis model is retired. Mzizi serves the\n        DNA double helix: nodes on an engineering backbone and a meaning\n        backbone, held together by cross-cutting rungs. There are no axes, no\n        outliers, no 3D and no X/Y/Z.\n\n        Wrapped `get_axes_summary()`, which returned four rows — horizontal / vertical / depth / outlier —\n        with every count zeroed after the helix migration.\n\n        Retired rather than remapped — emitting strand data through an\n        axis-shaped field would look correct and teach the wrong model to every\n        consumer that read it.\n\n        Replaced by:\n        - `GET /architecture` — the helix snapshot\n        - MCP `get_node_counts` — per-node counts\n      operationId: architecture-axes-gone\n      tags: [Architecture]\n      responses:\n        "410":\n          description: Gone — the axis model is retired.\n          headers:\n            Cache-Control:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CachePublic"\n            Access-Control-Allow-Origin:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CorsWildcard"\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                properties:\n                  error:\n                    type: string\n                    example: Gone\n                  message:\n                    type: string\n                  model:\n                    type: string\n                    example: mzizi-dna-helix\n                  migrated_to:\n                    type: object\n                    additionalProperties:\n                      type: string\n\n  /architecture/nodes/{n}:\n    get:\n      summary: Per-node detail (covenant, stakeholder, rules, component count)\n      description: |\n        One element of the DNA double helix — a node on a strand or a cross-cutting\n        rung — with its covenant, stakeholder, implementation rules, strand, backbone\n        and live component count. Reads\n        `component_documents` / `documentation-architecture-nodes`.\n\n        **`n` has no upper bound.** Node numbers are labels, not a sequence, and the\n        set is never capped, so a `maximum` here would be the defect rather than a\n        validation — the `1-10` bound on the retired `/architecture/layers/{n}` is\n        exactly what made N11 unreachable. Whether `n` exists is answered by the\n        collection: a missing number is 404, not 400. 400 is reserved for input that\n        is not a positive integer at all.\n      operationId: getHelixNode\n      tags: [Architecture]\n      parameters:\n        - name: n\n          in: path\n          required: true\n          schema:\n            type: integer\n            minimum: 1\n      responses:\n        "200":\n          description: Node or rung detail with covenant, stakeholder, and rules.\n          headers:\n            Cache-Control:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CachePublic"\n            Access-Control-Allow-Origin:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CorsWildcard"\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                properties:\n                  data: {type: object}\n                  meta:\n                    type: object\n                    properties:\n                      model: {type: string, example: mzizi-dna-helix}\n                      version: {type: string}\n        "400":\n          description: "`n` is not a positive integer."\n        "404":\n          $ref: "#/components/responses/NotFound"\n\n  /architecture/layers/{n}:\n    get:\n      summary: Per-layer detail (retired)\n      description: |\n        **HTTP 410 Gone — retired.** Wrapped `get_layer_detail(p_layer_number int)`\n        and served an `axis_name` on every row behind a `1-10` bound. Both halves\n        were the retired model: nothing belongs to an axis because there are none,\n        and the node set is never capped — that bound is what made N11 unreachable.\n\n        Retired rather than kept as a stable alias. The `layers` segment was\n        previously preserved "for URL stability", and a stable URL serving retired\n        vocabulary is how the drift spread.\n\n        Replaced by:\n        - `GET /architecture/nodes/{n}` — the same unit, uncapped, no axis field\n        - `GET /architecture` — the whole helix\n        - MCP `get_node_documents` — the live node/strand documents\n\n        The SITE path `/architecture/layers/{n}` is a permanent redirect to\n        `/architecture/nodes/{n}`, so a human following an old link still lands on\n        the page.\n      operationId: architecture-layers-gone\n      tags: [Architecture]\n      parameters:\n        - name: n\n          in: path\n          required: true\n          schema:\n            type: integer\n            minimum: 1\n      responses:\n        "410":\n          description: Gone — the layer model is retired.\n          headers:\n            Cache-Control:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CachePublic"\n            Access-Control-Allow-Origin:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CorsWildcard"\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                properties:\n                  error:\n                    type: string\n                    example: Gone\n                  message:\n                    type: string\n                  model:\n                    type: string\n                    example: mzizi-dna-helix\n                  migrated_to:\n                    type: object\n                    additionalProperties:\n                      type: string\n\n  /architecture/frontend/axes:\n    get:\n      summary: Frontend axes (retired)\n      description: |\n        **HTTP 410 Gone — retired.** The axis model is retired. Mzizi serves the\n        DNA double helix: nodes on an engineering backbone and a meaning\n        backbone, held together by cross-cutting rungs. There are no axes, no\n        outliers, no 3D and no X/Y/Z.\n\n        Served one row per axis with a `geometry` field carrying horizontal / vertical / depth / external.\n\n        Retired rather than remapped — emitting strand data through an\n        axis-shaped field would look correct and teach the wrong model to every\n        consumer that read it.\n\n        Replaced by:\n        - `GET /architecture` — the helix snapshot\n        - MCP `get_node_documents`\n      operationId: architecture-frontend-axes-gone\n      tags: [Architecture]\n      responses:\n        "410":\n          description: Gone — the axis model is retired.\n          headers:\n            Cache-Control:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CachePublic"\n            Access-Control-Allow-Origin:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CorsWildcard"\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                properties:\n                  error:\n                    type: string\n                    example: Gone\n                  message:\n                    type: string\n                  model:\n                    type: string\n                    example: mzizi-dna-helix\n                  migrated_to:\n                    type: object\n                    additionalProperties:\n                      type: string\n\n  /architecture/frontend/layers:\n    get:\n      summary: Frontend layers (retired)\n      description: |\n        **HTTP 410 Gone — retired.** The axis model is retired. Mzizi serves the\n        DNA double helix: nodes on an engineering backbone and a meaning\n        backbone, held together by cross-cutting rungs. There are no axes, no\n        outliers, no 3D and no X/Y/Z.\n\n        Served `layerNumber` / `subLabel` / `axisName` per row — layer-era vocabulary in which every unit belonged to an axis.\n\n        Retired rather than remapped — emitting strand data through an\n        axis-shaped field would look correct and teach the wrong model to every\n        consumer that read it.\n\n        Replaced by:\n        - `GET /architecture/nodes/{n}` — per-node detail\n        - MCP `get_node_documents` — live node and strand documents\n      operationId: architecture-frontend-layers-gone\n      tags: [Architecture]\n      responses:\n        "410":\n          description: Gone — the axis model is retired.\n          headers:\n            Cache-Control:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CachePublic"\n            Access-Control-Allow-Origin:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CorsWildcard"\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                properties:\n                  error:\n                    type: string\n                    example: Gone\n                  message:\n                    type: string\n                  model:\n                    type: string\n                    example: mzizi-dna-helix\n                  migrated_to:\n                    type: object\n                    additionalProperties:\n                      type: string\n\n  /ubuntu/pillars:\n    get:\n      summary: Ubuntu Pillars\n      description: |\n        The five Ubuntu Pillars — spheres in which Ubuntu is lived. Each pillar\n        maps a region of life to a platform surface so the doctrine translates\n        to software. Sourced from the `ubuntu_pillars` table.\n      operationId: getUbuntuPillars\n      tags: [Ubuntu]\n      responses:\n        "200":\n          description: Ubuntu pillars\n          headers:\n            Cache-Control:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CachePublic"\n            Access-Control-Allow-Origin:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CorsWildcard"\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: "#/components/schemas/UbuntuPillarsResponse"\n        "500":\n          $ref: "#/components/responses/InternalError"\n\n  /ubuntu/principles:\n    get:\n      summary: Ubuntu Principles\n      description: |\n        The five Ubuntu Principles — operating rules that translate Ubuntu to\n        software engineering decisions. Sourced from the `ubuntu_principles` table.\n      operationId: getUbuntuPrinciples\n      tags: [Ubuntu]\n      responses:\n        "200":\n          description: Ubuntu principles\n          headers:\n            Cache-Control:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CachePublic"\n            Access-Control-Allow-Origin:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CorsWildcard"\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: "#/components/schemas/UbuntuPrinciplesResponse"\n        "500":\n          $ref: "#/components/responses/InternalError"\n\n  /docs:\n    get:\n      summary: "GONE — long-form documentation moved into the repo as MDX"\n      description: |\n        Always returns HTTP 410 Gone.\n\n        Long-form documentation now lives in the repo as MDX (CLAUDE.md §15.18).\n        The `documentation_pages` Supabase table is HISTORICAL — content was\n        migrated in PR #57. The response body carries a `migrated_to` map that\n        lists the live URL for each former slug.\n      operationId: listDocs\n      deprecated: true\n      tags: [Content]\n      responses:\n        "410":\n          description: Gone — see `migrated_to` for live URLs.\n          headers:\n            Cache-Control:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CachePublic"\n            Access-Control-Allow-Origin:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CorsWildcard"\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                properties:\n                  error: {type: string, example: "Gone"}\n                  message: {type: string}\n                  migrated_to:\n                    type: object\n                    additionalProperties: {type: string, format: uri}\n\n  /docs/{slug}:\n    get:\n      summary: "GONE — see /docs for the migration map"\n      description: |\n        Always returns HTTP 410 Gone. See `GET /v1/docs` for the\n        per-slug → URL migration map.\n      operationId: getDoc\n      deprecated: true\n      tags: [Content]\n      parameters:\n        - name: slug\n          in: path\n          required: true\n          schema: {type: string}\n      responses:\n        "410":\n          description: Gone — see /docs for the migration map.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                properties:\n                  error: {type: string, example: "Gone"}\n                  message: {type: string}\n                  slug: {type: string}\n\n  /changelog:\n    get:\n      summary: List releases\n      description: >-\n        Every release, newest first, classified. Reads the `releases` view rather\n        than the `changelog` table: ordering that table by `released_at` put ten\n        undated 4.1.x rows above the current 1.0.0, because Postgres sorts NULLS\n        FIRST on DESC. Ordering by semver instead would put 4.2.0 above 1.0.0,\n        which is equally wrong — the version line was deliberately reset. `line`\n        carries the era and the response is pre-sorted by it.\n      operationId: listChangelog\n      tags: [Content]\n      responses:\n        "200":\n          description: Release list\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                properties:\n                  data:\n                    type: array\n                    items:\n                      $ref: "#/components/schemas/ChangelogEntry"\n                  meta:\n                    type: object\n                    properties:\n                      total: {type: integer}\n\n  /changelog/{version}:\n    get:\n      summary: Get every entry published under a version\n      description: >-\n        `data` is an ARRAY: a version number is not unique. Eight of them carry\n        two or three entries with different titles and content (4.0.31 has\n        three). This route used a single-row query, and PostgREST answers the\n        same error code for "more than one row" as for "no rows", so those\n        eight versions answered 404 for a release that exists. The first entry\n        is also spread at the top level so consumers written against the older\n        single-object shape keep working.\n      operationId: getRelease\n      tags: [Content]\n      parameters:\n        - name: version\n          in: path\n          required: true\n          schema: {type: string, example: "4.0.31"}\n      responses:\n        "200":\n          description: Every entry published under this version\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                allOf:\n                  - $ref: "#/components/schemas/ChangelogEntry"\n                  - type: object\n                    properties:\n                      data:\n                        type: array\n                        items:\n                          $ref: "#/components/schemas/ChangelogEntry"\n                      meta:\n                        type: object\n                        properties:\n                          version: {type: string}\n                          entries: {type: integer}\n        "404":\n          $ref: "#/components/responses/NotFound"\n\n  /skills:\n    get:\n      summary: List published skills\n      description: |\n        Returns every skill (agent-skill MDX bodies) from the registry\'s\n        published skills bundle, in the lightweight summary shape (no `body_mdx`).\n        Use `GET /skills/{name}` to fetch a single skill\'s full body.\n\n        Skills are reusable workflows AI assistants invoke on specific\n        tasks. Distinct from `/ai/instructions`, which serve per-AI-target\n        system prompts.\n      operationId: listSkills\n      tags: [Content]\n      responses:\n        "200":\n          description: "Skill index in `{ data: SkillSummary[], meta: { count } }`"\n          headers:\n            Cache-Control:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CachePublic"\n            Access-Control-Allow-Origin:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CorsWildcard"\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                properties:\n                  data:\n                    type: array\n                    items:\n                      type: object\n                      properties:\n                        name: {type: string}\n                        description: {type: string}\n                        agents:\n                          type: array\n                          items: {type: string}\n                        applies_to:\n                          type: array\n                          items: {type: string}\n                        requires_mcp: {type: boolean}\n                        version: {type: string}\n                        status: {type: string, nullable: true}\n                        updated_at: {type: string, format: date-time}\n                  meta:\n                    type: object\n                    properties:\n                      count: {type: integer}\n\n  /skills/summary:\n    get:\n      summary: Lightweight skill index for the CLI update path\n      description: |\n        The same document as `GET /skills`. Reserved for clients that\n        detect version drift cheaply (`meta.version`); gives `/skills`\n        headroom to add filtering or pagination later without breaking\n        that contract.\n      operationId: getSkillsSummary\n      tags: [Content]\n      responses:\n        "200":\n          description: Skill summary index.\n          headers:\n            Cache-Control:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CachePublic"\n            Access-Control-Allow-Origin:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CorsWildcard"\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                properties:\n                  data:\n                    type: array\n                    items: {type: object}\n                  meta:\n                    type: object\n                    properties:\n                      count: {type: integer}\n\n  /skills/{name}:\n    get:\n      summary: Get a single skill (with full body_mdx)\n      description: |\n        Returns the full skill row including `body_mdx`. Used by\n        consumers that need to write the skill to disk or pipelines\n        doing direct `curl` against the API.\n\n        Validates `name` against `^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$`. Returns 400 on\n        invalid pattern, and 404 when the name is well-formed but no\n        skill has it.\n      operationId: getSkill\n      tags: [Content]\n      parameters:\n        - name: name\n          in: path\n          required: true\n          description: Kebab-case skill name (e.g. `mzizi-design`)\n          schema:\n            type: string\n            pattern: "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$"\n      responses:\n        "200":\n          description: Skill with full `body_mdx` MDX content.\n          headers:\n            Cache-Control:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CachePublic"\n            Access-Control-Allow-Origin:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CorsWildcard"\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                properties:\n                  data:\n                    type: object\n                    properties:\n                      id: {type: integer}\n                      name: {type: string}\n                      description: {type: string}\n                      body_mdx: {type: string}\n                      agents:\n                        type: array\n                        items: {type: string}\n                      applies_to:\n                        type: array\n                        items: {type: string}\n                      requires_mcp: {type: boolean}\n                      version: {type: string}\n                      status: {type: string, nullable: true}\n                      created_at: {type: string, format: date-time}\n                      updated_at: {type: string, format: date-time}\n        "400":\n          description: Invalid skill name pattern.\n        "404":\n          $ref: "#/components/responses/NotFound"\n\n  /ai/instructions:\n    get:\n      summary: List AI instruction sets\n      description: |\n        Lists the AI instruction sets (system prompts for Claude projects, GitHub Copilot and the\n        MCP server), read from `content/doctrine/ai-instructions` in the registry. Use\n        `GET /ai/instructions/{name}` for one set\'s full text.\n      operationId: listAiInstructions\n      tags: [Content]\n      responses:\n        "200":\n          description: Instruction set index\n          headers:\n            Cache-Control:\n              schema:\n                type: string\n                example: "public, max-age=300, s-maxage=3600"\n            Access-Control-Allow-Origin:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CorsWildcard"\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [data, meta]\n                properties:\n                  data:\n                    type: array\n                    items:\n                      type: object\n                      required: [name, target]\n                      properties:\n                        name: {type: string, example: "nyuchi-mcp-system-prompt"}\n                        target: {type: string, example: "mcp-server"}\n                        title: {type: string, description: "Present only when the doctrine row has one."}\n                        description: {type: string}\n                        version: {type: string, example: "2.4"}\n                        updated_at: {type: string, description: "Present only when the doctrine row has one."}\n                  meta:\n                    type: object\n                    properties:\n                      total: {type: integer}\n        "500":\n          $ref: "#/components/responses/InternalError"\n\n  /ai/instructions/{name}:\n    get:\n      summary: Get an AI instruction set by name or target\n      description: |\n        Returns one instruction set\'s doctrine row in full, including `instruction_text`.\n        `name` is matched against the set\'s name first (e.g. `nyuchi-mcp-system-prompt`), then\n        against its target (e.g. `mcp-server`, `github-copilot`, `claude-system-prompt`).\n      operationId: getAiInstruction\n      tags: [Content]\n      parameters:\n        - name: name\n          in: path\n          required: true\n          description: An instruction set\'s name or its target.\n          schema: {type: string, example: "mcp-server"}\n      responses:\n        "200":\n          description: Instruction set (the doctrine row, as authored)\n          headers:\n            Cache-Control:\n              schema:\n                type: string\n                example: "public, max-age=300, s-maxage=3600"\n            Access-Control-Allow-Origin:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CorsWildcard"\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [name, target, instruction_text]\n                additionalProperties: true\n                properties:\n                  name: {type: string, example: "nyuchi-mcp-system-prompt"}\n                  target: {type: string, example: "mcp-server"}\n                  description: {type: string}\n                  version: {type: string, example: "2.4"}\n                  currentVersion: {type: integer}\n                  doctrineVersion: {type: string}\n                  kind: {type: string, example: "ai_instruction"}\n                  status: {type: string, example: "active"}\n                  owner: {type: string}\n                  model: {type: string, example: "mzizi-dna-helix"}\n                  node: {type: integer}\n                  strand: {type: string}\n                  dnaRole: {type: string}\n                  applies_to_categories:\n                    type: array\n                    items: {type: string}\n                  instruction_text: {type: string, description: "Full instruction text"}\n        "404":\n          description: No instruction set has this name or target\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: "#/components/schemas/Error"\n              example: {error: \'AI instruction "claude" not found\'}\n        "500":\n          $ref: "#/components/responses/InternalError"\n\n  /search:\n    get:\n      summary: Search components\n      description: |\n        Searches the registry on disk. `q` is a case-insensitive substring of a component\'s\n        name or description, `node` is its node on the helix, and `category` is one of its\n        `categories`. Parameters combine (AND), and at least one is required.\n      operationId: search\n      tags: [Discovery]\n      parameters:\n        - name: q\n          in: query\n          required: false\n          description: Case-insensitive substring of the name or description.\n          schema: {type: string, example: "button"}\n        - name: node\n          in: query\n          required: false\n          description: Node number on the helix, as written (e.g. `2`).\n          schema: {type: string, example: "2"}\n        - name: category\n          in: query\n          required: false\n          description: One of the component\'s `categories`.\n          schema: {type: string}\n        - name: layer\n          in: query\n          required: false\n          deprecated: true\n          description: |\n            Deprecated alias of `node`, kept so older clients keep their results. When it is\n            used (and `node` is not), the response carries `meta.deprecation` and a\n            `Deprecation: true` header. `node` wins when both are given. It will be removed.\n          schema: {type: string}\n      responses:\n        "200":\n          description: Matching components, in registry order\n          headers:\n            Cache-Control:\n              schema:\n                type: string\n                example: "public, max-age=300, s-maxage=3600"\n            Access-Control-Allow-Origin:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CorsWildcard"\n            Deprecation:\n              description: "`true` when the request filtered with the deprecated `layer` parameter."\n              schema: {type: string, example: "true"}\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [data, meta]\n                properties:\n                  data:\n                    type: array\n                    items:\n                      type: object\n                      required: [name]\n                      properties:\n                        name: {type: string}\n                        type: {type: string, example: "registry:ui"}\n                        title: {type: string}\n                        description: {type: string}\n                        categories:\n                          type: array\n                          items: {type: string}\n                        node: {type: integer}\n                        nodeLabel: {type: string}\n                  meta:\n                    type: object\n                    required: [total, query, node, category]\n                    properties:\n                      total: {type: integer}\n                      query: {type: [string, "null"]}\n                      node: {type: [string, "null"]}\n                      category: {type: [string, "null"]}\n                      deprecation:\n                        type: string\n                        description: Present only when the deprecated `layer` parameter was used.\n        "400":\n          description: None of q, node (or layer) and category was given\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: "#/components/schemas/Error"\n              example: {error: "At least one of q, node, or category is required"}\n        "500":\n          $ref: "#/components/responses/InternalError"\n\n  /stats:\n    get:\n      summary: Public usage statistics (open data — CC BY 4.0)\n      description: |\n        The public usage dataset — aligned with the bundu open data philosophy.\n        Usage telemetry is not part of the registry\'s files, so the aggregate\n        counts (calls, errors, latency, top components, top tools) are zero.\n        `layers` holds the real per-node component counts, derived from the\n        registry on disk. Carries schema.org `Dataset` JSON-LD + CC BY 4.0\n        license. Never hardcoded.\n      operationId: getStats\n      tags: [Discovery]\n      parameters:\n        - name: days\n          in: query\n          required: false\n          description: "Lookback period in days. Clamped to [1, 90]."\n          schema:\n            type: integer\n            minimum: 1\n            maximum: 90\n            default: 30\n      responses:\n        "200":\n          description: Stats\n          headers:\n            Cache-Control:\n              schema:\n                type: string\n                example: "public, max-age=60, s-maxage=120"\n            Access-Control-Allow-Origin:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CorsWildcard"\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                properties:\n                  "@context": {type: string, const: "https://schema.org"}\n                  "@type": {type: string, const: "Dataset"}\n                  name: {type: string}\n                  description: {type: string}\n                  license: {type: string, format: uri}\n                  total_api_calls: {type: integer}\n                  total_mcp_calls: {type: integer}\n                  layers:\n                    type: object\n                    additionalProperties: {type: integer}\n        "500":\n          $ref: "#/components/responses/InternalError"\n\n  /ui/{name}/docs:\n    get:\n      summary: Get component documentation\n      description: |\n        A component\'s documentation, built from the `meta` block of its item in\n        `registry.json`: use cases, variants, sizes, features, accessibility notes and\n        examples, plus whether it ships a hand-written demo.\n      operationId: getComponentDocs\n      tags: [Registry]\n      parameters:\n        - name: name\n          in: path\n          required: true\n          schema: {type: string, example: "button"}\n      responses:\n        "200":\n          description: Component documentation\n          headers:\n            Cache-Control:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CachePublic"\n            Access-Control-Allow-Origin:\n              $ref: "#/components/headers/CorsWildcard"\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [name, docs, demo]\n                properties:\n                  name: {type: string}\n                  description: {type: string}\n                  node: {type: integer}\n                  nodeLabel: {type: string}\n                  owner: {type: string}\n                  collection: {type: string}\n                  docs:\n                    type: [object, "null"]\n                    properties:\n                      id: {type: integer, description: "Always 0: the docs come from a file, not a row."}\n                      component_name: {type: string}\n                      use_cases:\n                        type: array\n                        items: {type: string}\n                      variants:\n                        type: array\n                        items: {type: string}\n                      sizes:\n                        type: array\n                        items: {type: string}\n                      features:\n                        type: array\n                        items: {type: string}\n                      a11y:\n                        type: array\n                        items: {type: string}\n                      examples:\n                        type: array\n                        items: {type: object}\n                      created_at: {type: string, description: "Always empty: the manifest\'s history is git\'s."}\n                      updated_at: {type: string, description: "Always empty: the manifest\'s history is git\'s."}\n                  demo:\n                    type: [object, "null"]\n                    description: Present when the component ships a hand-written demo.\n                    properties:\n                      id: {type: integer}\n                      component_name: {type: string}\n                      has_demo: {type: boolean}\n                      demo_type: {type: [string, "null"]}\n                      created_at: {type: string}\n                      updated_at: {type: string}\n        "404":\n          description: Component not found\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: "#/components/schemas/Error"\n        "500":\n          $ref: "#/components/responses/InternalError"\n\n  /ui/{name}/versions:\n    get:\n      summary: Component version history (not served)\n      description: |\n        Always 503. Component version history is machine-written data owned by the Mzizi\n        console, not part of the registry\'s files, and this API has no database. Release\n        history is at `GET /v1/changelog`.\n      operationId: getComponentVersions\n      tags: [Registry]\n      parameters:\n        - name: name\n          in: path\n          required: true\n          schema: {type: string}\n      responses:\n        "503":\n          $ref: "#/components/responses/ServiceUnavailable"\n\n  /mcp:\n    post:\n      summary: MCP JSON-RPC\n      description: |\n        Model Context Protocol endpoint for AI assistants. Accepts JSON-RPC requests\n        using the Streamable HTTP transport. Exposes registry components, brand system,\n        design tokens, and architecture data as MCP resources and tools.\n      operationId: mcpJsonRpc\n      tags: [MCP]\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              required: [jsonrpc, method]\n              properties:\n                jsonrpc:\n                  type: string\n                  const: "2.0"\n                method:\n                  type: string\n                  description: "MCP method (e.g., tools/list, tools/call, resources/read)"\n                id:\n                  oneOf:\n                    - type: string\n                    - type: integer\n                params:\n                  type: object\n      responses:\n        "200":\n          description: JSON-RPC response\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [jsonrpc]\n                properties:\n                  jsonrpc:\n                    type: string\n                    const: "2.0"\n                  id:\n                    oneOf:\n                      - type: string\n                      - type: integer\n                  result:\n                    type: object\n                  error:\n                    type: object\n                    properties:\n                      code:\n                        type: integer\n                      message:\n                        type: string\n    get:\n      summary: MCP SSE Stream\n      description: Server-Sent Events stream for MCP notifications.\n      operationId: mcpSse\n      tags: [MCP]\n      responses:\n        "200":\n          description: SSE event stream\n          content:\n            text/event-stream:\n              schema:\n                type: string\n    delete:\n      summary: MCP Session Cleanup\n      description: Cleans up an MCP session.\n      operationId: mcpCleanup\n      tags: [MCP]\n      responses:\n        "200":\n          description: Session cleaned up\n    options:\n      summary: MCP CORS Preflight\n      description: CORS preflight for MCP endpoint.\n      operationId: mcpCors\n      tags: [MCP]\n      responses:\n        "204":\n          description: CORS headers returned\n\ncomponents:\n  headers:\n    CachePublic:\n      schema:\n        type: string\n        example: "public, max-age=3600, s-maxage=86400"\n    CorsWildcard:\n      schema:\n        type: string\n        example: "*"\n\n  schemas:\n    Error:\n      type: object\n      required: [error]\n      properties:\n        error:\n          type: string\n\n    ServiceUnavailableError:\n      type: object\n      required: [error]\n      properties:\n        error:\n          type: string\n          example: "Version history is not served by this API"\n        message:\n          type: string\n          description: Why the data is not served, and where to look instead.\n\n    # ── Discovery ──────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n    ApiDiscovery:\n      type: object\n      required: ["@context", "@type", name, version, description, homepage, resources]\n      properties:\n        $schema:\n          type: string\n          example: "https://mzizi.dev/schema/api.json"\n        "@context":\n          type: string\n          const: "https://schema.org"\n        "@type":\n          type: string\n          const: "WebAPI"\n        name:\n          type: string\n          example: "Mzizi API"\n        version:\n          type: string\n          example: "1.0.0"\n        description:\n          type: string\n        homepage:\n          type: string\n          format: uri\n          example: "https://mzizi.dev"\n        data:\n          type: object\n          description: Where the data comes from. There is no database; the files are the data layer.\n          properties:\n            source: {type: string, const: "files"}\n            repository: {type: string, format: uri, example: "https://github.com/mzizi-dev/mzizi-registry"}\n            components: {type: integer, description: "Live registry count."}\n        resources:\n          type: object\n          additionalProperties:\n            type: object\n            required: [href, description]\n            properties:\n              href:\n                type: string\n              description:\n                type: string\n\n    # ── Brand ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n    BrandSystem:\n      type: object\n      required:\n        [\n          $schema,\n          version,\n          name,\n          minerals,\n          heritage,\n          experimental,\n          ecosystem,\n          typography,\n          spacing,\n        ]\n      properties:\n        $schema:\n          type: string\n          example: "https://mzizi.dev/schema/brand.json"\n        "@context":\n          type: string\n          const: "https://schema.org"\n        "@type":\n          type: string\n          const: "Brand"\n        version:\n          type: string\n          example: "4.0.40"\n        name:\n          type: string\n          example: "The Mzizi Brand System"\n        lastUpdated:\n          type: string\n          format: date\n          example: "2026-03-09"\n        homepage:\n          type: string\n          format: uri\n          example: "https://mzizi.dev/brand"\n        minerals:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: "#/components/schemas/Mineral"\n        heritage:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: "#/components/schemas/HeritageColor"\n        experimental:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: "#/components/schemas/ExperimentalColor"\n        ecosystem:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: "#/components/schemas/EcosystemBrand"\n        typography:\n          type: object\n          required: [fonts, scale]\n          properties:\n            fonts:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties:\n                $ref: "#/components/schemas/FontSpec"\n            scale:\n              type: array\n              items:\n                $ref: "#/components/schemas/TypeScaleEntry"\n        spacing:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: "#/components/schemas/SpacingToken"\n        radii:\n          type: object\n          additionalProperties:\n            type: string\n        semanticColors:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: "#/components/schemas/SemanticColor"\n        backgrounds:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: "#/components/schemas/BackgroundToken"\n        componentSpecs:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: "#/components/schemas/ComponentSpec"\n        accessibility:\n          $ref: "#/components/schemas/Accessibility"\n        voiceAndTone:\n          $ref: "#/components/schemas/VoiceAndTone"\n        philosophy:\n          $ref: "#/components/schemas/Philosophy"\n\n    ColorFamily:\n      type: object\n      description: |\n        The fields every colour family carries (minerals, heritage tones and\n        experimental tones), from `lib/tokens/palette.generated.ts`.\n        `lightHex` and `darkHex` are the canonical accents and fills, not text\n        values. For text in this colour on the page use `textLight` /\n        `textDark`, measured as text on `--base` (APCA Lc 75). Where the\n        canonical value already clears that bar, `textLight` equals `lightHex`\n        (and `textDark` equals `darkHex`).\n      required: [name, hex, lightHex, darkHex, cssVar]\n      properties:\n        name:\n          type: string\n          example: "cobalt"\n        hex:\n          $ref: "#/components/schemas/Hex"\n          description: |\n            The family\'s single default value. For minerals it is\n            `mineralApiHex` in `lib/tokens/brand.source.ts`; for heritage and\n            experimental tones it is `darkHex`.\n        lightHex:\n          $ref: "#/components/schemas/Hex"\n        darkHex:\n          $ref: "#/components/schemas/Hex"\n        textLight:\n          $ref: "#/components/schemas/Hex"\n          description: |\n            The family as text on `--base`, light theme: the light value of\n            `--color-<name>-text` in `mzizi-tokens-globals.css`, from\n            `textOnBaseTier()` in `scripts/render-globals-css.ts`.\n        textDark:\n          $ref: "#/components/schemas/Hex"\n          description: |\n            The family as text on `--base`, dark theme: the dark value of\n            `--color-<name>-text`.\n        cssVar:\n          type: string\n          example: "--color-cobalt"\n\n    Mineral:\n      description: |\n        A mineral: the `MineralToken` in `lib/tokens/palette.generated.ts`,\n        plus `hex` and the `-text` pair. Text on the mineral\'s container uses\n        `onContainerLight` / `onContainerDark`.\n        `lightHex` and `darkHex` are the canonical accents and fills, not text\n        values. For text in this colour on the page use `textLight` /\n        `textDark`, measured as text on `--base` (APCA Lc 75). Where the\n        canonical value already clears that bar, `textLight` equals `lightHex`\n        (and `textDark` equals `darkHex`).\n      allOf:\n        - $ref: "#/components/schemas/ColorFamily"\n        - type: object\n          required: [origin, symbolism, usage]\n          properties:\n            role:\n              type: string\n              example: "Knowledge"\n            family:\n              $ref: "#/components/schemas/MineralFamily"\n            containerLight:\n              $ref: "#/components/schemas/Hex"\n              description: Light theme container background for this mineral\n            containerDark:\n              $ref: "#/components/schemas/Hex"\n              description: Dark theme container background for this mineral\n            onContainerLight:\n              $ref: "#/components/schemas/Hex"\n              description: Text colour on the light theme container\n            onContainerDark:\n              $ref: "#/components/schemas/Hex"\n              description: Text colour on the dark theme container\n            sortOrder:\n              type: integer\n              minimum: 0\n              description: Position among the minerals\n            origin:\n              type: string\n              description: African origin of this mineral\n            symbolism:\n              type: string\n            usage:\n              type: string\n\n    HeritageColor:\n      description: |\n        A heritage tone (`heritageColors` in `lib/tokens/palette.generated.ts`),\n        plus `hex` (its `darkHex`) and the `-text` pair.\n        `lightHex` and `darkHex` are the canonical accents and fills, not text\n        values. For text in this colour on the page use `textLight` /\n        `textDark`, measured as text on `--base` (APCA Lc 75). Where the\n        canonical value already clears that bar, `textLight` equals `lightHex`\n        (and `textDark` equals `darkHex`).\n      allOf:\n        - $ref: "#/components/schemas/ColorFamily"\n        - type: object\n          required: [origin, symbolism, usage]\n          properties:\n            origin:\n              type: string\n            symbolism:\n              type: string\n            usage:\n              type: string\n\n    ExperimentalColor:\n      description: |\n        An experimental tone (`experimentalColors` in\n        `lib/tokens/palette.generated.ts`), plus `hex` (its `darkHex`), `cssVar`\n        and the `-text` pair. Text on its container uses `onContainerLight` /\n        `onContainerDark`; `uiLight` / `uiDark` are its UI tints.\n        `lightHex` and `darkHex` are the canonical accents and fills, not text\n        values. For text in this colour on the page use `textLight` /\n        `textDark`, measured as text on `--base` (APCA Lc 75). Where the\n        canonical value already clears that bar, `textLight` equals `lightHex`\n        (and `textDark` equals `darkHex`).\n      allOf:\n        - $ref: "#/components/schemas/ColorFamily"\n        - type: object\n          required:\n            [\n              containerLight,\n              containerDark,\n              onContainerLight,\n              onContainerDark,\n              uiLight,\n              uiDark,\n              heptagonIndex,\n            ]\n          properties:\n            containerLight:\n              $ref: "#/components/schemas/Hex"\n            containerDark:\n              $ref: "#/components/schemas/Hex"\n            onContainerLight:\n              $ref: "#/components/schemas/Hex"\n              description: Text colour on the light theme container\n            onContainerDark:\n              $ref: "#/components/schemas/Hex"\n              description: Text colour on the dark theme container\n            uiLight:\n              $ref: "#/components/schemas/Hex"\n            uiDark:\n              $ref: "#/components/schemas/Hex"\n            heptagonIndex:\n              type: integer\n              minimum: 0\n              description: The tone\'s position on the experimental heptagon\n\n    MineralFamily:\n      type: string\n      enum: ["deep-earth", "hand"]\n      description: The mineral\'s family\n\n    Hex:\n      type: string\n      pattern: "^#[0-9A-Fa-f]{6}$"\n      example: "#0047AB"\n\n    EcosystemBrand:\n      type: object\n      required: [name, meaning, language, role, mineral, url]\n      properties:\n        name:\n          type: string\n          example: "mukoko"\n        meaning:\n          type: string\n        language:\n          type: string\n          example: "Shona"\n        role:\n          type: string\n        description:\n          type: string\n        voice:\n          type: string\n        mineral:\n          type: string\n          description: The brand\'s palette family (usually a mineral)\n        url:\n          type: string\n          format: uri\n        displayName:\n          type: string\n          description: |\n            The product name people read, where it is not the wordmark `name`\n            (e.g. "Mukoko Events" for `events`). Present only on the rows that\n            have one.\n        accent:\n          type: string\n          description: |\n            A second palette family for `--brand-accent`, where the brand pairs\n            one with its `mineral` (e.g. `circles`: tanzanite with a terracotta\n            accent). Present only on the rows that have one.\n        aliases:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            type: string\n          description: |\n            Deprecated names that still resolve to this row (e.g. `nhimbe` for\n            `events`). Present only on the rows that have them; never use one in\n            new code.\n\n    FontSpec:\n      type: object\n      required: [family, usage, reason]\n      properties:\n        family:\n          type: string\n          example: "Noto Sans"\n        usage:\n          type: string\n        reason:\n          type: string\n\n    TypeScaleEntry:\n      type: object\n      required: [name, sizePx, sizeRem, lineHeight, weight, font, usage]\n      properties:\n        name:\n          type: string\n        sizePx:\n          type: number\n        sizeRem:\n          type: string\n        lineHeight:\n          type: string\n        weight:\n          type: integer\n        font:\n          type: string\n          enum: ["sans", "serif", "mono"]\n        usage:\n          type: string\n\n    SpacingToken:\n      type: object\n      required: [name, px, rem, usage]\n      properties:\n        name:\n          type: string\n        px:\n          type: number\n        rem:\n          type: string\n        usage:\n          type: string\n\n    SemanticColor:\n      type: object\n      required: [name, light, dark, usage]\n      properties:\n        name:\n          type: string\n        light:\n          type: string\n        dark:\n          type: string\n        usage:\n          type: string\n\n    BackgroundToken:\n      type: object\n      required: [name, light, dark, usage]\n      properties:\n        name:\n          type: string\n        light:\n          type: string\n        dark:\n          type: string\n        usage:\n          type: string\n\n    ComponentSpec:\n      type: object\n      required: [name, heights, padding, borderRadius, minTouchTarget, variants]\n      properties:\n        name:\n          type: string\n        heights:\n          type: object\n          additionalProperties:\n            type: number\n        padding:\n          type: string\n        borderRadius:\n          type: number\n        minTouchTarget:\n          type: number\n          minimum: 48\n        variants:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            type: string\n\n    Accessibility:\n      type: object\n      required: [standard, minTouchTarget]\n      properties:\n        standard:\n          type: string\n          example: "APCA 3.0 AAA"\n        contrastDescription:\n          type: string\n        minTouchTarget:\n          type: integer\n          minimum: 48\n        focusIndicator:\n          type: string\n        keyboardNavigation:\n          type: string\n        screenReaders:\n          type: string\n\n    VoiceAndTone:\n      type: object\n      required: [principles, doList, dontList]\n      properties:\n        principles:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            type: string\n        doList:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            type: string\n        dontList:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            type: string\n\n    Philosophy:\n      type: object\n      required: [name, meaning, pillars]\n      properties:\n        name:\n          type: string\n          example: "Ubuntu"\n        meaning:\n          type: string\n          example: "I am because we are"\n        pillars:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            type: object\n            required: [name, description]\n            properties:\n              name:\n                type: string\n              description:\n                type: string\n\n    # ── Registry ───────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n    RegistryIndex:\n      type: object\n      required: [$schema, name, homepage, items]\n      properties:\n        $schema:\n          type: string\n          const: "https://ui.shadcn.com/schema/registry.json"\n        name:\n          type: string\n          example: "mukoko"\n        homepage:\n          type: string\n          format: uri\n          example: "https://mzizi.dev"\n        items:\n          type: array\n          minItems: 1\n          items:\n            $ref: "#/components/schemas/RegistryItemSummary"\n\n    RegistryItemSummary:\n      type: object\n      required: [name, type, description, dependencies, registryDependencies]\n      properties:\n        name:\n          type: string\n          example: "button"\n        type:\n          type: string\n          enum: ["registry:ui", "registry:hook", "registry:lib"]\n        description:\n          type: string\n        dependencies:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            type: string\n        registryDependencies:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            type: string\n\n    RegistryItem:\n      type: object\n      required: [$schema, name, type, description, dependencies, registryDependencies, files]\n      properties:\n        $schema:\n          type: string\n          const: "https://ui.shadcn.com/schema/registry-item.json"\n        name:\n          type: string\n        type:\n          type: string\n          enum: ["registry:ui", "registry:hook", "registry:lib"]\n        description:\n          type: string\n        dependencies:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            type: string\n        registryDependencies:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            type: string\n        files:\n          type: array\n          minItems: 1\n          items:\n            $ref: "#/components/schemas/RegistryFile"\n\n    RegistryFile:\n      type: object\n      required: [path, type, content]\n      properties:\n        path:\n          type: string\n          example: "components/ui/button.tsx"\n        type:\n          type: string\n          example: "registry:ui"\n        content:\n          type: string\n          description: Full source code of the component file\n\n    # ── Architecture ───────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n    EcosystemArchitecture:\n      type: object\n      required: ["@context", "@type", name, principles, frameworkDecision]\n      properties:\n        "@context":\n          type: string\n          const: "https://schema.org"\n        "@type":\n          type: string\n          const: "TechArticle"\n        name:\n          type: string\n          example: "Mukoko Ecosystem Architecture"\n        principles:\n          type: array\n          minItems: 5\n          items:\n            $ref: "#/components/schemas/ArchitecturePrinciple"\n        frameworkDecision:\n          $ref: "#/components/schemas/FrameworkDecision"\n\n    ArchitecturePrinciple:\n      type: object\n      required: [name, title, description, rationale, implementation]\n      properties:\n        name:\n          type: string\n        title:\n          type: string\n        description:\n          type: string\n        rationale:\n          type: string\n        implementation:\n          type: string\n\n    FrameworkDecision:\n      type: object\n      required: [name, approach, framework, rationale, sovereigntyAdvantage, platforms, harmonyOs]\n      properties:\n        name:\n          type: string\n        approach:\n          type: string\n        framework:\n          type: string\n        rationale:\n          type: string\n        sovereigntyAdvantage:\n          type: string\n        platforms:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: "#/components/schemas/PlatformTarget"\n        harmonyOs:\n          type: object\n          required: [approach, rationale, status]\n          properties:\n            approach:\n              type: string\n            rationale:\n              type: string\n            status:\n              type: string\n\n    PlatformTarget:\n      type: object\n      required: [name, strategy, status]\n      properties:\n        name:\n          type: string\n        strategy:\n          type: string\n        status:\n          type: string\n          enum: ["production", "planned", "research"]\n\n    DataLayerArchitecture:\n      type: object\n      required: ["@context", "@type", name, localDataLayer, cloudLayer, dataOwnership]\n      properties:\n        "@context":\n          type: string\n          const: "https://schema.org"\n        "@type":\n          type: string\n          const: "TechArticle"\n        name:\n          type: string\n          example: "Mukoko Data Layer Architecture"\n        localDataLayer:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: "#/components/schemas/DataLayerTechnology"\n        cloudLayer:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: "#/components/schemas/CloudService"\n        dataOwnership:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: "#/components/schemas/DataOwnershipRule"\n\n    DataLayerTechnology:\n      type: object\n      required: [name, role, platform, description, sovereignty]\n      properties:\n        name:\n          type: string\n        role:\n          type: string\n        platform:\n          type: string\n          enum: ["native", "browser", "both"]\n        description:\n          type: string\n        sovereignty:\n          $ref: "#/components/schemas/SovereigntyAssessment"\n\n    CloudService:\n      type: object\n      required: [name, role, consistencyModel, database, dataCategories, description, sovereignty]\n      properties:\n        name:\n          type: string\n        role:\n          type: string\n        consistencyModel:\n          type: string\n          enum: ["strict", "eventual"]\n        database:\n          type: string\n        dataCategories:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            type: string\n        description:\n          type: string\n        sovereignty:\n          $ref: "#/components/schemas/SovereigntyAssessment"\n\n    DataOwnershipRule:\n      type: object\n      required: [category, consistencyModel, database, examples, ownership, description]\n      properties:\n        category:\n          type: string\n        consistencyModel:\n          type: string\n          enum: ["strict", "eventual", "aggregate"]\n        database:\n          type: string\n        examples:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            type: string\n        conflictResolution:\n          type: string\n        ownership:\n          type: string\n          enum: ["user-private", "community-shared", "public-open"]\n        description:\n          type: string\n\n    PipelineArchitecture:\n      type: object\n      required: ["@context", "@type", name, stages]\n      properties:\n        "@context":\n          type: string\n          const: "https://schema.org"\n        "@type":\n          type: string\n          const: "TechArticle"\n        name:\n          type: string\n          example: "Mukoko Open Data Pipeline"\n        stages:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: "#/components/schemas/PipelineStage"\n\n    PipelineStage:\n      type: object\n      required: [name, role, description, sovereignty]\n      properties:\n        name:\n          type: string\n        role:\n          type: string\n        description:\n          type: string\n        sovereignty:\n          $ref: "#/components/schemas/SovereigntyAssessment"\n\n    SovereigntyReport:\n      type: object\n      required: ["@context", "@type", name, assessments, removedTechnologies]\n      properties:\n        "@context":\n          type: string\n          const: "https://schema.org"\n        "@type":\n          type: string\n          const: "TechArticle"\n        name:\n          type: string\n          example: "Mukoko Technology Sovereignty"\n        assessments:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: "#/components/schemas/SovereigntyAssessment"\n        removedTechnologies:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: "#/components/schemas/RemovedTechnology"\n\n    SovereigntyAssessment:\n      type: object\n      required:\n        [technology, role, license, governance, sovereigntyRisk, forkable, selfHostable, rationale]\n      properties:\n        technology:\n          type: string\n        role:\n          type: string\n        license:\n          type: string\n        governance:\n          type: string\n        sovereigntyRisk:\n          type: string\n          enum: ["none", "low", "removed"]\n        forkable:\n          type: boolean\n        selfHostable:\n          type: boolean\n        rationale:\n          type: string\n\n    RemovedTechnology:\n      type: object\n      required: [name, previousRole, reason, replacement, migrationPath]\n      properties:\n        name:\n          type: string\n        previousRole:\n          type: string\n        reason:\n          type: string\n        replacement:\n          type: string\n        migrationPath:\n          type: string\n\n    # ── Health ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n    HealthStatus:\n      type: object\n      required: [status, timestamp, checks, version]\n      properties:\n        status:\n          type: string\n          enum: ["healthy", "degraded", "unhealthy"]\n        timestamp:\n          type: string\n          format: date-time\n        checks:\n          type: object\n          required: [registry, filesystem]\n          properties:\n            registry:\n              $ref: "#/components/schemas/HealthCheck"\n            filesystem:\n              $ref: "#/components/schemas/HealthCheck"\n        version:\n          type: string\n\n    HealthCheck:\n      type: object\n      required: [status, latencyMs]\n      properties:\n        status:\n          type: string\n          enum: ["pass", "fail"]\n        latencyMs:\n          type: integer\n        message:\n          type: string\n        itemCount:\n          type: integer\n\n    UbuntuPillar:\n      type: object\n      required: [name, shona, title, description, sphere, platformSurface, source]\n      properties:\n        name: {type: string}\n        shona: {type: string, description: "Shona-language name"}\n        title: {type: string}\n        description: {type: string}\n        sphere: {type: string, description: "Region of life the pillar covers"}\n        platformSurface: {type: string, description: "Software surface the pillar maps to"}\n        source: {type: string, description: "Origin citation for the pillar"}\n        sortOrder: {type: integer}\n\n    UbuntuPillarsResponse:\n      type: object\n      required: ["@context", "@type", name, itemListElement]\n      properties:\n        "@context": {type: string}\n        "@type": {type: string, example: "ItemList"}\n        name: {type: string}\n        description: {type: string}\n        itemListElement:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: "#/components/schemas/UbuntuPillar"\n\n    UbuntuPrinciple:\n      type: object\n      required: [name, shona, title, description, expression, source]\n      properties:\n        name: {type: string}\n        shona: {type: string}\n        title: {type: string}\n        description: {type: string}\n        expression: {type: string, description: "How the principle shows up in software"}\n        source: {type: string}\n        sortOrder: {type: integer}\n\n    UbuntuPrinciplesResponse:\n      type: object\n      required: ["@context", "@type", name, itemListElement]\n      properties:\n        "@context": {type: string}\n        "@type": {type: string, example: "ItemList"}\n        name: {type: string}\n        description: {type: string}\n        itemListElement:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: "#/components/schemas/UbuntuPrinciple"\n\n    # ── Content (docs + changelog) ────────────────────────────────\n\n    DocPageSummary:\n      type: object\n      required: [slug, title]\n      properties:\n        slug: {type: string}\n        title: {type: string}\n        summary: {type: string}\n        layer: {type: integer, nullable: true}\n        updatedAt: {type: string, format: date-time}\n\n    DocPage:\n      allOf:\n        - $ref: "#/components/schemas/DocPageSummary"\n        - type: object\n          properties:\n            body: {type: string, description: "Long-form markdown/MDX content"}\n\n    ChangelogEntry:\n      type: object\n      required: [version, title, description, changed_by, created_at, released_at]\n      properties:\n        version: {type: string, example: "4.0.40"}\n        title: {type: string}\n        description: {type: string}\n        line:\n          type: string\n          enum: [public, "pre-1.0"]\n          description: >-\n            Which version era this release belongs to. `public` is the 1.x line;\n            `pre-1.0` is the internal 4.x iteration that 1.0.0 superseded. Both\n            live in one table, which is why no single sort key orders the\n            changelog correctly.\n        line_rank:\n          type: integer\n          description: "Sort weight for `line` — public outranks pre-1.0."\n        major: {type: integer, nullable: true}\n        minor: {type: integer, nullable: true}\n        patch: {type: integer, nullable: true}\n        release_kind:\n          type: string\n          enum: [initial, major, minor, patch]\n          description: >-\n            Compared to the predecessor within the SAME line — a patch bump in\n            4.1.x is not a major bump merely because 1.0.0 exists.\n        breaking: {type: boolean, nullable: true}\n        components_touched:\n          type: integer\n          description: "components_added + modified + deprecated + removed."\n        nodes_affected:\n          type: array\n          description: >-\n            Nodes and rungs of the DNA double helix touched by this release.\n            No upper bound: node numbers are labels, not a sequence, and the\n            set is never capped.\n          items: {type: integer, minimum: 1}\n        components_added:\n          type: array\n          items: {type: string}\n        components_modified:\n          type: array\n          items: {type: string}\n        components_deprecated:\n          type: array\n          items: {type: string}\n        components_removed:\n          type: array\n          items: {type: string}\n        tools_added:\n          type: array\n          description: "Mzizi tools — MCP tools, SDK helpers — added in this release."\n          items: {type: string}\n        tools_modified:\n          type: array\n          items: {type: string}\n        tools_deprecated:\n          type: array\n          items: {type: string}\n        tools_removed:\n          type: array\n          items: {type: string}\n        linked_issues:\n          type: array\n          description: "GitHub issue / PR numbers referenced by this release."\n          items: {type: integer}\n        total_stable: {type: integer, nullable: true}\n        total_deprecated: {type: integer, nullable: true}\n        total_alpha: {type: integer, nullable: true}\n        changed_by: {type: string}\n        created_at: {type: string, format: date-time}\n        released_at: {type: string, format: date-time}\n\n  responses:\n    InternalError:\n      description: Internal server error\n      content:\n        application/json:\n          schema:\n            $ref: "#/components/schemas/Error"\n    NotFound:\n      description: Resource not found\n      content:\n        application/json:\n          schema:\n            $ref: "#/components/schemas/Error"\n    ServiceUnavailable:\n      description: Data this API does not serve, because it is not part of the registry\'s files\n      content:\n        application/json:\n          schema:\n            $ref: "#/components/schemas/ServiceUnavailableError"\n';
